---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & Contributing — DIGIWIKI"
  description="How this wiki works and how to add your own pages."
>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>About this wiki</h1>
    <p>
      DIGIWIKI is a static site built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>.
      Every page is a plain <strong>Markdown file</strong>; Astro turns them into
      fast HTML pages with validated frontmatter, automatic sidebar grouping,
      prev/next links and an offline-capable search index.
    </p>

    <h2>Add a new page in 30 seconds</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Create a file in <code>src/content/digimon/</code> — its name becomes the URL
        (e.g. <code>biyomon.md</code> → <code>/wiki/biyomon</code>).</li>
      <li>Paste the frontmatter below and fill it in.</li>
      <li>Write the body in normal Markdown.</li>
      <li>Save. The page instantly appears in the sidebar, the All Entries page,
        the search index, and gets prev/next links.</li>
    </ol>

    <pre><code>{`---
title: "Biyomon"
emoji: "🐦"
stage: "Rookie"           # Fresh | In-Training | Rookie | Champion | Ultimate | Mega
rank: "SSS"               # SSS+ | SSS | U
attribute: "Vaccine"      # Vaccine | Virus | Data
role: "Skill"             # Autoattack | Skill | Tank
partner: "Sora Takenouchi"
description: "A bird Digimon whose wings have degenerated…"
tags: ["adventure", "partner"]
order: 20                 # position in lists / prev-next flow
---

## Overview

Anything you write here is rendered as rich Markdown.`}</code></pre>

    <h2>Frontmatter fields</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Field</th><th>Required</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>title</code></td><td>✅</td><td>Page name everywhere on the site</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>emoji</code></td><td>—</td><td>Avatar shown on cards/sidebar (default 🥚)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>stage</code></td><td>—</td><td>Evolution stage used for grouping</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>rank</code></td><td>—</td><td>Rarity rank: SSS+ / SSS / U</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>attribute</code></td><td>—</td><td>Vaccine / Virus / Data</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>role</code></td><td>—</td><td>Combat type: Autoattack / Skill / Tank</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>partner</code></td><td>—</td><td>Human partner, if any</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>description</code></td><td>✅</td><td>Short summary for cards + search</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tags</code></td><td>—</td><td>List of free-form keywords</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>order</code></td><td>—</td><td>Sort position (default 99)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="muted">
      Invalid frontmatter fails the build with a helpful error — that's the content
      collection schema keeping the wiki consistent.
    </p>

    <h2>Re-theming</h2>
    <p>
      The whole look lives in <code>src/styles/global.css</code> under
      <code>:root</code> — swap <code>--bg</code>, <code>--accent</code>,
      <code>--accent-2</code> etc. and the entire site reskins itself.
    </p>

    <h2>Accessories collection</h2>
    <p>
      Gear lives in <code>src/content/accessories/</code> and appears at
      <code>/accessories</code> with its own sidebar, category filter and detail
      pages. Frontmatter:
    </p>

    <pre><code>{`---
title: "Taichi's Goggles"
emoji: "🥽"
category: "Goggles"   # Goggles | Digivice | Equipment | Cloth
owner: "Tai Kamiya"   # optional
description: "Short summary for cards & search."
tags: ["goggles"]
order: 10             # position within its category
---`}</code></pre>

    <blockquote>
      <strong>Note:</strong> Digimon™ is a trademark of Bandai / Akiyoshi Hongo.
